id: decisions/018-who-may-authorise
title: "principal authority or agent autonomy"
kind: decision-frame
record_shape: header
status: draft
authored_by: agent-on-behalf
authored_via: "Claude Code session on Dave's behalf, 2026-09-12; drafted from the JUDGMENTS.md reversal axis 'who-may-authorise'; recommendation is an attributed inference and ratifies nothing"
version: "1.0.0"
updated: 2026-09-12
template_ref: templates/decision.yawn
principal_ref: principal:dave

axis: who-may-authorise
axis_gloss: "whether an effect needs a named human principal's say-so, or an agent/automation may license its own action"
poles:
  a: principal-authority
  b: agent-autonomy
split: lone-exception
draft_status: axis-only
leverage: 13.9
leverage_formula: "judgments_resolved(29) x split_weight(0.4) x authored_conflict_bonus(1.2)"

question: >
  On who may authorise — whether an effect needs a named human principal's
  say-so, or an agent/automation may license its own action — the records assert
  both principal authority (27 judgments, 22 authored) and agent autonomy (2
  judgments, 0 authored). Which should be the stated rule, and where is the
  exception?

why_it_matters: >
  Until this is answered, a record below Dave inherits whichever side it happens
  to copy. Full draft pending: the proposal batch for this axis did not
  complete; the axis, poles, counts and evidence are real, the options below are
  the generic form.

state_snapshot:
  description: >
    27 judgments sit at principal-authority (22 authored) and 2 at agent-autonomy
    (0 authored). The repository asserts both directions on this axis.
  attributed_to: JUDGMENTS.md
  epistemic_status: observed
  source_refs:
    - JUDGMENTS.md
    - TAXONOMY.md

lacuna:
  kind: unselected_choice
  description: >
    The full proposal.

options:
  - name: A
    description: >
      principal authority becomes the stated rule across its scope.
    cost: "not yet drafted"
    risk: "not yet drafted"
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "not yet drafted"
    evidence_for:
      - "J0005"
      - "J0014"
      - "J0022"
      - "J0030"
      - "J0113"
      - "J0139"
  - name: B
    description: >
      agent autonomy becomes the stated rule across its scope.
    cost: "not yet drafted"
    risk: "not yet drafted"
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "not yet drafted"
    evidence_for:
      - "J0397"
      - "J0545"
  - name: C
    description: >
      One pole is the rule; the other is a written carve-out for a named case.
    cost: "not yet drafted"
    risk: "not yet drafted"
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "not yet drafted"
    evidence_for:
      []

recommendation:
  option_ref: 
  confidence: 0
  epistemic_status: inferred
  authority: none
  reasoning: >
    Not drafted. Re-run the decision-proposal workflow for this axis; the
